  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The focus of the given parabola is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The centre of the circle with two focal chords as tangent is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/9a707980-2361-4fd0-8c4a-3ea1bca2b5ac.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.89375in;height:1.7in\" /></p><p>From the figure,&nbsp;</p><p>the distance between the centre of the circle and the focus is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;units</p><p>Hence, the radius of the circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
